  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 20,
    "summary": "Zophar shows the condition of the wicked—He says, The triumphing of the wicked is short, and the joy of the hypocrite is but for a moment.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then answered Zophar the Naamathite, and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore do my thoughts cause me to answer, and for this I make haste.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "I have heard the check of my reproach, and the spirit of my understanding causeth me to answer.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowest thou not this of old, since man was placed upon earth,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "That the triumphing of the wicked is short, and the joy of the hypocrite but for a moment?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Joy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Joy.",
            "prettyString": "TG Joy",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Joy",
                "entryId": "tg-joy",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Though his excellency mount up to the heavens, and his head reach unto the clouds;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet he shall perish for ever like his own dung: they which have seen him shall say, Where is he?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 92
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall fly away as a dream, and shall not be found: yea, he shall be chased away as a vision of the night.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "The eye also which saw him shall see him no more; neither shall his place any more behold him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "His children shall seek to please the poor, and his hands shall restore their goods.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "His bones are full of the sin of his youth, which shall lie down with him in the dust.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "TG Carnal Mind."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 26
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Carnal Mind.",
            "prettyString": "TG Carnal Mind",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Carnal Mind",
                "entryId": "tg-carnal-mind",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Though wickedness be sweet in his mouth, though he hide it under his tongue;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Though he spare it, and forsake it not; but keep it still within his mouth:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet his meat in his bowels is turned, it is the gall of asps within him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath swallowed down riches, and he shall vomit them up again: God shall cast them out of his belly.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall suck the poison of asps: the viper’s tongue shall slay him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall not see the rivers, the floods, the brooks of honey and butter.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "That which he laboured for shall he restore, and shall not swallow it down: according to his substance shall the restitution be, and he shall not rejoice therein.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          },
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 92
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 108
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 128
          },
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 162
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Because he hath oppressed and hath forsaken the poor; because he hath violently taken away an house which he builded not;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Surely he shall not feel quietness in his belly, he shall not save of that which he desired.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "There shall none of his meat be left; therefore shall no man look for his goods.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "In the fulness of his sufficiency he shall be in straits: every hand of the wicked shall come upon him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "When he is about to fill his belly, God shall cast the fury of his wrath upon him, and shall rain it upon him while he is eating.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 100
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall flee from the iron weapon, and the bow of steel shall strike him through.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "It is drawn, and cometh out of the body; yea, the glittering sword cometh out of his gall: terrors are upon him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 102
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "All darkness shall be hid in his secret places: a fire not blown shall consume him; it shall go ill with him that is left in his tabernacle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "The heaven shall reveal his iniquity; and the earth shall rise up against him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "The increase of his house shall depart, and his goods shall flow away in the day of his wrath.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "This is the portion of a wicked man from God, and the heritage appointed unto him by God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 20:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 29
      }
    ]
